## Substitute $x = 2$
\text{Expression} &= \frac{3(2)+5}{10} - \frac{1}{2+3}
&= \frac{6+5}{10} - \frac{1}{5}
&= \frac{11}{10} - \frac{1}{5}
## Write over a common denominator and subtract
The common denominator is $10$, and $\frac{1}{5} = \frac{2}{10}$.
&= \frac{11}{10} - \frac{2}{10}
&= \frac{9}{10}
ANSWER: \frac{9}{10}

## Relate $g'(x)$ to the graph
$g$ is a straight line, so $g'(x)$ is its slope, the same everywhere.
## Read two points from the graph
The line passes through $(0, 1)$ and $(6, 5)$.
## Use rise over run
m &= \frac{5 - 1}{6 - 0}
&= \frac{4}{6}
&= \frac{2}{3}
ANSWER: g'(x) = \frac{2}{3}

## Read the graph at 08:00
Go up from 08:00 on the time axis to the line, then across to the distance axis. Mark these guide lines on the diagram.
\text{distance} &\approx 13 \text{ km}
ANSWER: 13 \ \text{km}

## Write the speed formula
S &= \frac{D}{T}
## Find the distance from A to B
D &= 32 - 20
&= 12 \text{ km}
## Find the time from A to B
A is at 08:30 and B is at 09:00, so the time is 30 minutes.
T &= 30 \text{ min} = 0.5 \text{ hours}
## Divide distance by time
S &= \frac{12}{0.5}
&= 24
ANSWER: 24 \ \text{km/hour}

## Find the total grams of carbon for the flight
\text{total} &= 28\,000 \times 394
&= 11\,032\,000 \text{ g}
## Divide by the number of passengers
\text{per passenger} &= \frac{11\,032\,000}{244}
&\approx 45\,213.11 \text{ g}
## Convert grams to kilograms
There are 1000 g in 1 kg, so divide by 1000.
\text{per passenger} &= \frac{45\,213.11}{1000}
&\approx 45.2131 \text{ kg}
## Round to 1 decimal place
&\approx 45.2 \text{ kg}
ANSWER: 45.2 \ \text{kg}

## Count the even-numbered cards
The even numbers are 2, 4 and 6, and each appears in both colours.
\text{Even cards} &= 3 + 3
&= 6
## Write the probability
Probability = favourable outcomes $\div$ total outcomes.
P(\text{even}) &= \frac{6}{14}
&= \frac{3}{7}
ANSWER: \frac{3}{7}
